  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 136 AM MDT Thu Sep 24 2026\n\nSaturday begins the weekend and long term period with a significant \ndown tick in rain chances with drying conditions. Sunday sees an \napproaching upper trough axis dig southward across the western \nCONUS. This feature, alongside Hurricane Polo will act to advect \nmore monsoonal moisture northward into the AZ/NM, allowing for \nafternoon shower and thunderstorm development to favor eastern AZ \ninto western NM Sunday afternoon. Thereafter, the trough axis is \nfavored to track across NM either Monday or Tuesday with significant \ndivergence being resolved b/w various numerical model suites. The \ndepth of the trough digging over the Desert Southwest will play a \nmajor role for just how much precipitation breaks out and and how \nfast storms move west to east across the state. Any resulting flash \nflooding risk will be the result of a balancing act between the \ncoverage of showers/storms and how fast they move. Drier conditions \nmove into the area in the wake of this feature either mid or late \nnext week.",
